<template>
    <children><li id="44.lp5"/><li id="43.lp5"/></children>
    <heading>Storage</heading>
    <keywords><li>storage</li><li>filesystem</li><li>HTTP</li><li>cancellation</li></keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>This unit provides whole-file storage for projects through <code>storage.local</code> and <code>storage.remote</code>. Each <code>open</code> method returns an independent project object with <code>root_filename</code>, <code>load(filename, signal?)</code>, <code>store(filename, text)</code>, <code>remove(filename)</code>, and <code>list_files(signal?)</code>. The directory handle or URL stays private. Filenames are single relative names; subdirectories are outside this interface.</p>
        <p>All operations return Promises and reject on failure. <code>load</code> returns complete text; <code>store</code> creates or replaces a complete text file; <code>list_files</code> returns sorted immediate file names. Missing-file removal rejects. Listing does not reserve a name, so concurrent creation of an unused article filename needs a later exclusive-create contract. Neither backend promises transactions or rollback across files.</p>
        <p>This unit does not select directories, persist selections, or change the current model. The selecting operation supplies an opened storage object to the model; the model does not inspect its location.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code"><name>JavaScript units</name><code><![CDATA[
let storage = (() => {
    const locations = new WeakMap();

    function filename(name) {
        if (typeof name !== "string" || !name || name === "." || name === ".." ||
            /[\x00-\x1f\x7f/\\<>:"|?*]/.test(name) || /[. ]$/.test(name))
            throw new Error(`Invalid storage filename: ${name}`);
        return name;
    }

    function project(backend, location, root_filename) {
        const result = Object.create(backend);
        Object.defineProperty(result, "root_filename", {
            value: filename(root_filename), enumerable: true
        });
        locations.set(result, location);
        return result;
    }

    function location(object) {
        if (!locations.has(object)) throw new Error("Open a storage project first");
        return locations.get(object);
    }

]]><lp5- ref="Local storage backend"/><lp5- ref="Remote storage backend"/><![CDATA[    return { local, remote };
})();
]]></code></section>
</template>
